  "slug": "microbe-comprehensive-mapping-583d",
  "summary": "Sequence-based coevolution and enzyme-constrained metabolic models now predict bacterial interactomes and kinetics across species.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is coupling learned or sequence-based predictors to mechanistic and constraint-based layers to infer bacterial function. ContextMirror2.0 predicts species-specific interactomes for E. coli, S. enterica and S. aureus from sequence coevolution, while kinGEMs feeds CPI-Pred kcat predictions into an uncertainty-aware pipeline for enzyme-constrained metabolic models across 93 organisms. GEM-CM pairs reaction-diffusion modelling with random-forest surrogates of genome-scale metabolic models to simulate P. aeruginosa PA14 in gel environments. BacLLM fuses UniProt annotation priors into protein language models for antimicrobial resistance analysis, and amino acid clustering with epistasis informs sequence-based phenotype prediction. What is new is the explicit combination of predictive models with mechanistic simulation and annotation priors, extending functional assignment from individual proteins toward organism-level and spatially resolved simulation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
